# Copy to .env.local for local development. .env* files are gitignored.
#
# Variable taxonomy:
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the browser bundle. They are
#   public by design — never put secrets behind the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# - Everything else is server-side only and must never appear in client
#   code, docs, tests, CI, or logs.

# Pooled Postgres connection string for runtime queries (Neon pooled
# endpoint, e.g. ...-pooler....neon.tech). SECRET — never commit.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require

# Direct (unpooled) connection string used by prisma migrate deploy /
# introspection / seed scripts. SECRET — never commit.
# DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=postgresql://user:password@host.region.aws.neon.tech/dbname?sslmode=require

# Non-secret hostname of the PRODUCTION database. Set on the Preview
# environment only: scripts/vercel-build.ts uses it as an exclusion
# check so a preview deployment can never run migrations against
# production. A missing value skips preview migrations (fail-safe).
# APP_PRODUCTION_DB_HOST=host.region.aws.neon.tech

# Isolated database for *.db.test.ts suites — a dedicated test database
# (e.g. docker-compose local postgres or a Neon dev branch), never the
# dev or preview database you work against interactively.
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/sarbase_test

# Canonical site origin (canonical URLs, Open Graph, sitemap, robots).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.com

# Canonical app origin — also gates the Secure flag on the session
# cookie (https:// => Secure; also forced for VERCEL_ENV production/preview).
# APP_BASE_URL=https://example.com

# --- Authentication (Firebase Auth) — see docs/authentication.md ---
# Browser-side Firebase web app config. Public by design (NEXT_PUBLIC_*);
# these values identify the project, they are not credentials. When absent
# the sign-in UI reports "authentication is not configured" and every
# protected surface fails closed.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=<project>.firebaseapp.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Server-side Firebase Admin service-account credentials — used only to
# verify ID tokens and mint/revoke session cookies. SECRET — never commit;
# set in deployment env only. Paste the private key with \n escapes.
# FIREBASE_ADMIN_PROJECT_ID=
# FIREBASE_ADMIN_CLIENT_EMAIL=firebase-adminsdk-...@<project>.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# FIREBASE_ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# --- Observability (Sentry) — all optional; absent = fully disabled ---
# Server-side error reporting DSN. SECRET-adjacent (ingest credential);
# set in deployment environments, not in CI.
# SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@o<org>.ingest.<region>.sentry.io/<project>
# Browser error reporting DSN — public by design (NEXT_PUBLIC_*).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@o<org>.ingest.<region>.sentry.io/<project>
# Sourcemap upload credentials — set ONLY in the deployment environment
# (Vercel), never in CI. Without all three, builds skip sourcemap upload.
# SENTRY_ORG=
# SENTRY_PROJECT=
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
